{"data": [{"author_id": "21347707", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:53:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117419812590874626"], "id": "2117419812590874626", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator What I've seen as companies scale is that acceleration often moves the bottleneck. \n\nWhen producing code gets dramatically faster, testing, integration, and release discipline become even more important to execution.", "url": "https://x.com/JeffJamesMartin/status/2117419812590874626"}, {"author_id": "27814665", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:29:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117413772575064148"], "id": "2117413772575064148", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 295, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Thrilled to be supporting this team since they finished YC! Let's go @useblacksmith!", "url": "https://x.com/GVteam/status/2117413772575064148"}, {"author_id": "2092564080813088768", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:52:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117389505120624834"], "id": "2117389505120624834", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Same thing on the website side: shipping changes got fast, but checking that a change didn't slow a page down or break checkout is still the slow part.", "url": "https://x.com/NimbicaAI/status/2117389505120624834"}, {"author_id": "1639153825448890369", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:45:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117387539233558891"], "id": "2117387539233558891", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Focusing solely on speed might introduce new failure modes. How will Blacksmith ensure rapid CI doesn't sacrifice necessary depth in validation?", "url": "https://x.com/sophiaw63_y/status/2117387539233558891"}, {"author_id": "1460431504220332042", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:09:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117378652895604747"], "id": "2117378652895604747", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 23, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Renting servers built for Minecraft and Call of Duty was a brilliant start, since so much of a CI run is compile and test steps that reward single-core speed over core count, exactly what gaming CPUs are tuned for. A $1B CI cloud run by 30 people is impressive.", "url": "https://x.com/YuboZhao2008/status/2117378652895604747"}, {"author_id": "1776997292601647104", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:05:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117362361996910691"], "id": "2117362361996910691", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Testing becoming the bottleneck is the same story in ecommerce, just with a different name. AI can generate 20 product variants in an afternoon, but validating which one actually converts still takes real buyers and real time. I now run AI-generated listings through a 48-hour", "url": "https://x.com/andyliang17335/status/2117362361996910691"}, {"author_id": "1755477816479768576", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:55:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117359865622311016"], "id": "2117359865622311016", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator This matches what I see with AI-generated code: more tests, not fewer. The real win is faster feedback before a bad change blocks the whole team.", "url": "https://x.com/henry_luck99/status/2117359865622311016"}, {"author_id": "2957820500", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:05:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117347260803822079"], "id": "2117347260803822079", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Shorter test runs make it easier for an agent to work in small steps. When something breaks, there's less new code to untangle.", "url": "https://x.com/DavidWever/status/2117347260803822079"}, {"author_id": "1460014078609534976", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:39:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117340754515526020"], "id": "2117340754515526020", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Same shift is showing up outside software. Once AI makes the drafts fast, whether it's code, quotes or emails, checking the work becomes the slow part. Teams that set up a simple review step early tend to move faster later, not slower.", "url": "https://x.com/Laidzzx/status/2117340754515526020"}, {"author_id": "1881173355921108992", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:18:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117335611052880370"], "id": "2117335611052880370", "in_reply_to_user_id": "378292434", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117333611087081494", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Bijan_Automates @ycombinator Faster green builds are exactly what I pay for in my head, my agent loop stalls on CI and not on the model. I would trade a smarter model for a ten second test run without thinking twice.", "url": "https://x.com/harden_369741/status/2117335611052880370"}, {"author_id": "378292434", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:10:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117333611087081494"], "id": "2117333611087081494", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator As coding agents spit out more diffs the bottleneck moves to tests\n\nCutting CI from minutes to seconds is the unlock for agent loops\n\nWould you pay more for faster green builds than for a smarter model right now", "url": "https://x.com/Bijan_Automates/status/2117333611087081494"}, {"author_id": "2025569786441469952", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:49:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117328171691593983"], "id": "2117328171691593983", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Blacksmith proving gaming CPUs beat enterprise cloud bloat is pure Logic-over-Hardware.\n\nTrue architectural breakthroughs don't come from massive budgets; they come from outsiders ruthlessly optimizing constrained silicon.\n\nExecution beats pedigree. ♟️", "url": "https://x.com/ShihabiLogic/status/2117328171691593983"}, {"author_id": "206720696", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:27:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117322598854144392"], "id": "2117322598854144392", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator I'm already seeing this. The code shows up faster than anyone can check it, so testing becomes the real bottleneck.", "url": "https://x.com/cheneypiano/status/2117322598854144392"}, {"author_id": "206720696", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:26:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117322596815385080"], "id": "2117322596815385080", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator I'm already seeing this. The code shows up faster than anyone can check it, so testing becomes the real bottleneck.", "url": "https://x.com/cheneypiano/status/2117322596815385080"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:11:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117318589447536884"], "id": "2117318589447536884", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Writing code was never the whole job, it just hid the rest. Now that generation is cheap, the hours move to proving the code deserves to ship, and teams that planned only for faster writing will feel that shift first.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2117318589447536884"}, {"author_id": "1507653715158659076", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:45:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117312090511691811"], "id": "2117312090511691811", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator AI made writing code cheap. Now the real bottleneck is trusting what shipped.", "url": "https://x.com/iamayushrawat/status/2117312090511691811"}, {"author_id": "1067301255234666496", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:38:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117310425037480027"], "id": "2117310425037480027", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator agents flip CI from a gate into the inner loop. a 10 minute pipeline was fine when a human pushed a few times a day. an agent iterating dozens of times on one PR turns CI wait into most of the wall clock. fast reruns are agent infra now, not devops polish", "url": "https://x.com/saimrahdarii/status/2117310425037480027"}, {"author_id": "3322026632", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:36:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117309859456786522"], "id": "2117309859456786522", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator @garrytan You and @JohnWuestlbik2 are my go-to for dev tooling—faster CI from Blacksmith sounds promising.", "url": "https://x.com/keita_okamoto_/status/2117309859456786522"}, {"author_id": "1444967404405092354", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:34:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117309311156428971"], "id": "2117309311156428971", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator \"testing is the new bottleneck\" is so real. agents write the code in 2 minutes and then everyone waits 20 for CI", "url": "https://x.com/lokidotdev/status/2117309311156428971"}, {"author_id": "7577952", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:24:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117306863880479160"], "id": "2117306863880479160", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 38, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator we saw this exact pattern at persona haha ,  the faster code gets written, the more testing becomes the thing people actually complain about at dinners", "url": "https://x.com/edugiansante/status/2117306863880479160"}, {"author_id": "2019929179131699200", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:13:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117304140816925168"], "id": "2117304140816925168", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator AI writes the code in seconds, then CI takes forty minutes. Smart bet.", "url": "https://x.com/peteryantweets/status/2117304140816925168"}, {"author_id": "1050574914619678725", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:07:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117302571693957232"], "id": "2117302571693957232", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator congrats blacksmith. ci is where all that ai written code goes to sit in a queue, so faster ci feels overdue", "url": "https://x.com/theaihacker/status/2117302571693957232"}, {"author_id": "879674442", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:06:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117302221931172306"], "id": "2117302221931172306", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Makes sense. When AI writes code faster, slow CI becomes the new wait time. For small teams it matters even more, since there's no QA team to catch what agents miss.", "url": "https://x.com/Asif876Asif/status/2117302221931172306"}, {"author_id": "1112265596152877057", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:05:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117302207960002822"], "id": "2117302207960002822", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator Faster CI makes experimentation cheaper. The next useful measure is how quickly a team can turn a failing test into a verified fix.", "url": "https://x.com/Neeraj_Kumar222/status/2117302207960002822"}, {"author_id": "1755477816479768576", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:55:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117299624583323831"], "id": "2117299624583323831", "in_reply_to_user_id": "113130846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283089294520638", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ycombinator This matches what I'm seeing: AI makes writing code cheap, so the real cost moves to verifying it. Do teams now spend more time writing tests than features, or does faster CI just hide that shift?", "url": "https://x.com/henry_luck99/status/2117299624583323831"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "21347707", "name": "Jeff James Martin", "username": "JeffJamesMartin"}, {"id": "27814665", "name": "GV", "username": "GVteam"}, {"id": "2092564080813088768", "name": "Nimbica", "username": "NimbicaAI"}, {"id": "1639153825448890369", "name": "soph k,", "username": "sophiaw63_y"}, {"id": "1460431504220332042", "name": "Yubo Zhao", "username": "YuboZhao2008"}, {"id": "1776997292601647104", "name": "andy liang", "username": "andyliang17335"}, {"id": "1755477816479768576", "name": "henry", "username": "henry_luck99"}, {"id": "2957820500", "name": "David H. Wever", "username": "DavidWever"}, {"id": "1460014078609534976", "name": "Laidz", "username": "Laidzzx"}, {"id": "1881173355921108992", "name": "E1ev3n.", "username": "harden_369741"}, {"id": "378292434", "name": "Bijan | AI for Law Firms | Investor", "username": "Bijan_Automates"}, {"id": "2025569786441469952", "name": "مُحَمَّدٌ الشِّهَابِيُّ | Mohammed Al-Shihabi", "username": "ShihabiLogic"}, {"id": "206720696", "name": "Jon Cheney", "username": "cheneypiano"}, {"id": "46498861", "name": "Raúl Nogales 🇪🇸🇺🇸", "username": "raulnogales"}, {"id": "1507653715158659076", "name": "Ayush Rawat", "username": "iamayushrawat"}, {"id": "1067301255234666496", "name": "Saim Rahdari", "username": "saimrahdarii"}, {"id": "3322026632", "name": "Jason", "username": "keita_okamoto_"}, {"id": "1444967404405092354", "name": "Loki", "username": "lokidotdev"}, {"id": "7577952", "name": "Ed Giansante", "username": "edugiansante"}, {"id": "2019929179131699200", "name": "Pete Ryan", "username": "peteryantweets"}, {"id": "1050574914619678725", "name": "Cipher0k", "username": "theaihacker"}, {"id": "879674442", "name": "Asif", "username": "Asif876Asif"}, {"id": "1112265596152877057", "name": "Neeraj Kumar", "username": "Neeraj_Kumar222"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117419812590874626", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyi9dxawafv11d3eodyrwlha8vx", "oldest_id": "2117299624583323831", "result_count": 25}}